    {
      "title": "Sync event buffer can hold up to 10000 full peer-supplied InstantLocks of up to 48,780 inputs each",
      "file": "dash-spv/src/sync/instantsend/manager.rs",
      "line": 185,
      "description": "Each lock that passes the structure check emits an `InstantLockReceived` event that carries a full clone of the lock, including locks of an unknown cycle that were never signature checked. The sync event broadcast channel has 10000 slots and keeps each value until every subscriber has read it. With a slow subscriber, attacker locks near the new 48,780 input cap (about 1.75 MB of outpoints each) can hold many gigabytes, far more than the 500-entry pending queue.",
      "security": true,
